WikiRevision.Content:
==API Urls==
Form ID:  ([~/?ScreenId=TC.10.60.00|TC.10.60.00]) {br}    

The API Urls window is just for internal use.

WikiRevision.column:
==Purchase Orders== Form ID: ([~/?ScreenId=PO301000|PO301000]) {br}
====Document Details Tab==== TrueCommerce has added the TC Status as well as three User Defined Fields to the Document Details tab of the Purchase Order screen. These four fields provide storage location to which you can transfer data from Transaction Manager to Acumatica.
As part of this integration to Acumatica when transactions are exported from Transaction Manager to Acumatica, fields are passed to Acumatica with data that Acumatica doesn’t normally store.
{| cellspacing="0" cellpadding="4" border="1" |-style="text-align: center; background-color: #D0D0D0; " !Field !! Description |- ! User Defined Fields(1-3) | Any additional information that is sent in the inbound purchase order that is pertinent to your business can be stored in these user defined fields. |- ! TC Status | This field can be mapped to on the export of a Purchase Order Acknowledgement to indicate whether the trading partner has accepted, partially accepted or rejected the purchase order (EDI 850) that was sent to them. |}
====TrueCommerce Tab====
'''TrueCommerce UDF''': The TrueCommerce UDF section on the Purchase Order screen lists the fields that were originally passed from Transaction Manager to Acumatica during the Purchase order Update.
As part of this integration to Acumatica when transactions are exported from Transaction Manager to Acumatica, fields are passed to Acumatica with data that Acumatica doesn’t normally store. {| cellspacing="0" cellpadding="4" border="1" |-style="text-align: center; background-color: #D0D0D0; " !Field !! Description |- ! User Defined Fields(1-5) | Any additional information that is sent in the inbound purchase order that is pertinent to your business can be stored in these user defined fields. |- ! TC Status | This field can be mapped to on the export of a Purchase Order Acknowledgement to indicate whether the trading partner has accepted, partially accepted or rejected the line item on a purchase order (EDI 850) that was sent to them. |}
'''Transaction Status''': Support is added to provide visibility within Acumatica to see when documents have been sent to the Trading Partner. {| cellspacing="0" cellpadding="4" border="1" |-style="text-align: center; background-color: #D0D0D0; " !Field !! Description |- ! Purchase Order Status | UDF in Purchase Order to indicate the sent status of Purchase Order(850) in Transaction Manager. |}

