==TrueCommerce Activity Report==
Form ID:  ([~/?ScreenId=TC.64.00.80|TC.64.00.80]) {br}    

TrueCommerce Activity Report8 displays the Pulse Dashboard after you log on Foundry.

WikiRevision.column:
==Auto-Pack Template== Form ID: ([~/?ScreenId=TC301000|TC301000]) {br}
Auto-pack templates let you define special packaging rules that can then be assigned to Acumatica customers. You can define packaging rules by Pack Quantity and can set rules to package multiple items to a carton. You can create as many auto-pack templates as you'd like. They’ll need to be defined to the customer in the Customer Settings within the Sales Order module under the heading "Other" prior to packaging the shipments.
Acumatica uses the Box No value to determine if items should be packaged together. For example, if two AACOMPUT01 items and one AALEGO500 item will fit in a single package, but AAPOWERAID must be shipped in its own package a template could be created as shown below.
{| cellspacing="0" cellpadding="4" border="1" col span="2" |- | colspan="2" style="text-align: center; background-color: #D0D0D0; " | '''Auto-Pack Template ''' |- ! Template ID | The name of the template. |- ! Template Description |A brief description of the template. |- ! Inventory ID | The unique inventory ID from Acumatica. |- ! Pack Quantity | The maximum quantity to be packaged within each box. |- ! Box No | Use the same or unique box numbers to indicate what items (if any) should be packaged together. |- ! Unit of Measure | This field is pulled from the Sales Unit for the item set in Acumatica. |}

==Bills and Adjustments== Form ID: ([~/?ScreenId=AP301000|AP301000]) {br}
====Document Details Tab==== TrueCommerce has added 3 user defined fields to the Document Details tab of the Bills and Adjustments screen. These fields provide storage location to which you can transfer data from Transaction Manager to Acumatica.
{| cellspacing="0" cellpadding="4" border="1" |-style="text-align: center; background-color: #D0D0D0; " !Field !! Description |- ! User Defined Fields(1-3) | Any additional information that is sent in the inbound Bills that is pertinent to your business can be stored in these user defined fields. |} ====TrueCommerce Tab====
The TrueCommerce tab on the Bills and Adjustments screen lists the fields that were originally passed from Transaction Manager to Acumatica during the Bills create. {| cellspacing="0" cellpadding="4" border="1" |-style="text-align: center; background-color: #D0D0D0; " !Field !! Description |- ! User Defined Fields(1-5) | Any additional information that is sent in the inbound Bills that is pertinent to your business can be stored in these user defined fields. |}

==Login==
Form ID:  ([~/?ScreenId=TC103000|TC103000]) {br}    

User must connect their Acumatica to API and Foundry using their Foundry user credentials. TrueCommerce will check the SKU permission, get all the trading partner names and templates for the customer’s tenant based on their login.(The customer must have the labeling SKU as part of their Transaction Manager instance.) {br}   

The following is the steps to connect Acumatica to API and Foundry. {br}   
1. Select the Environment(Should be set to Production unless something is being tested in Staging) {br}   
2. Enter Foundry User Name {br}   
3. Enter Foundry Password {br}   
4. Enter Tenant {br}   
5. Select Transaction Status, Report or Labeling {br}   
6. Click Sign in {br}

{| cellspacing="0" cellpadding="4" border="1"
|- 
| colspan="2" style="text-align: center; background-color: #D0D0D0; " | '''Logon History'''
|-
! Report Logon History
| The last logon history for the Report. 
|-
! Transaction Status Logon History
| The last logon history for the Transaction Status. 
|-
! Label Logon History
| The last logon history for the Label. 
|}

WikiRevision.Content:
==Labeling Log== Form ID: ([~/?ScreenId=TC302000|TC302000]) {br}
This form is to show the labeling logs after you print the labels in the Shipment screen or Batch Print screen. When you fail to print the labels, please go to this screen to see the details error and the label xml. Then you can modify the field map according to the label xml.
{| cellspacing="0" cellpadding="4" border="1" |- | colspan="2" style="text-align: center; background-color: #D0D0D0; " | '''Labeling Log''' |- ! Log Name | The name of this Labeling log. |- ! Log Time | The date of this Labeling log created. |- ! Print Status | This is the print status. |- ! Error Message | The detail error message returned by TrueCommerce if the label printing is failed. |- ! Label Xml | This is the Label Xml you sent to TrueCommerce. You can check the Xml and modify the mapping. |}

WikiRevision.column:
==Shipments== Form ID: ([~/?ScreenId=SO302000|SO302000]) {br}
====Document Details Tab==== TrueCommerce has added the PO Line Number as well as three User Defined Fields to the Document Details tab of the Sales Order screen. These three fields provide storage location to which you can transfer data from Transaction Manager to Acumatica.
As part of this integration to Acumatica when transactions are exported from Transaction Manager to Acumatica, fields are passed to Acumatica with data that Acumatica doesn’t normally store.
{| cellspacing="0" cellpadding="4" border="1" |-style="text-align: center; background-color: #D0D0D0; " !Field !! Description |- ! User Define Fields(1-3) | Any additional information that is sent in the inbound purchase order that is pertinent to your business can be stored in these user defined fields. |- ! PO Line Number | The line number from the inbound purchase order. |} ====Packages Tab==== In order to support for ASNs, TrueCommerce added the ability to buildout packages in Acumatica. {br} {| cellspacing="0" cellpadding="4" border="1" |-style="text-align: center; background-color: #D0D0D0; " !Field !! Description |- ! Assign Pallet |This button allows you to assign Pallet ID(s) for which the packages are placed on. |- ! Delete Pallet | This button allows you to delete Pallet ID assignment(s) that were previously assigned. |- ! Auto Pack |Click the "Auto Pack" button to create packages for your shipment based on the logic you previously entered in the Item Package Settings or Auto-Pack Template screens. Note: If you plan to use the Auto Pack functionality, do not add package rows prior to clicking the "Auto Pack" button as they will automatically be created during the Auto Pack process. |- ! Generate GS1-128 | This button allows you to generate the GS1-128 for the packages according to the settings in the Form([~/?ScreenId=TC102010|TC102010]) or Form ([~/?ScreenId=TC103040|TC103040]). |- ! Clear GS1-128 | This button allows you to clear GS1-128 that were previously assigned. |- ! Print Selected | This button allows you to print the labels for the selected packages. |- ! Print All | This button allows you to print the labels for all packages. |- ! Tracking Number | This field stores the shipping tracking number. |- ! Custom Ref. Nbr. 1 / Custom Ref. Nbr. 2 |Any additional information that is sent in the inbound purchase order that is pertinent to your business can be stored in these Customer Reference fields. |- ! GS1-128 |The GS1-128 number is assigned by Transaction Manager when the Acumatica shipment is exported. This field can also be used to store the GS1-128 number when importing a detailed warehouse shipping advice (EDI 945). |- ! Pallet ID | ID of the pallet which includes current package. |- ! Pallet GS1-128 | GS1-128 of the pallet which includes current package. |- ! Print Status |This field indicates the print status of current package when using Acumatica to print labels. |- ! Last Print Time |This field indicates the last print time of current package when using Acumatica to print labels. |} ====TrueCommerce Tab==== '''TrueCommerce UDF''': The TrueCommerce UDF section on the Shipments screen lists the fields that were originally passed from Transaction Manager to Acumatica during the sales order creation. With the exception of the Purchase Order Number field, there currently is no standard matching field within Acumatica for the EDI Store Number, EDI Distribution Center and ASN Type. Therefore, the TrueCommerce UDF section has been added to the Integration with Acumatica to store this data. Additionally, five user defined fields have also been added to this section as the storage location to which customers can transfer data from Transaction Manager to Acumatica. {br} {| cellspacing="0" cellpadding="4" border="1" |-style="text-align: center; background-color: #D0D0D0; " !Field !! Description |- ! Purchase Order Number | The purchase order number can be stored in this field. |- ! EDI Store Number |The EDI store number from the inbound purchase order can be stored to Acumatica in this field. |- ! EDI Distribution Center | The EDI distribution center from the inbound purchase order can be stored to Acumatica in this field. |- ! EDI Department Number |The EDI department number from the inbound purchase order can be stored to Acumatica in this field. |- ! User Defined Fields (1-5) | Any additional information that is sent in the inbound purchase order that is pertinent to your business can be stored in these user defined fields. |- ! ASN Type |Provides the option of No Pack, Pick & Pack, Standard, Pallet Pick & Pack, Pallet Standard, Pacejet Cloud No Pack, Pacejet Cloud Pick & Pack, Pacejet Cloud Standard, Pacejet Cloud Pallet Pick & Pack or Pacejet Cloud Pallet Standard ASN types to be imported into Transaction Manager and sent to your trading partner. This field will take precedence over the option set in Transaction Manager. |- ! Auto Pack |Click the "Auto Pack" button to create packages for your shipment based on the logic you previously entered in the Item Package Settings or Auto-Pack Template screens. |- ! Label Partner |During the Sales Order creation it’s possible to pass these values in when exporting a Purchase Order from Transaction Manager. It will be brought to Shipment from Sales Order. |- ! Label Template |During the Sales Order creation it’s possible to pass these values in when exporting a Purchase Order from Transaction Manager. It will be brought to Shipment from Sales Order. |- ! Print Destination |Select a printer that has been configured using the Acumatica Device Hub for label printing. |}
'''Ship-from Address''': The Ship From Address for label printing can be set when creating the sales order during the PO export from TM. It will be brought to Shipment from Sales Order. {| cellspacing="0" cellpadding="4" border="1" |-style="text-align: center; background-color: #D0D0D0; "" !Field !! Description |- ! Name | The name of the partner can be stored in this field. |- ! Address Line 1 | The address of the partner can be stored in this field. |- ! Address Line 2 | The address of the partner can be stored in this field. |- ! City | The city of the partner can be stored in this field. |- ! Country | The country of the partner can be stored in this field. |- ! State | The state of the partner can be stored in this field. |- ! Postal Code | The postal code of the partner can be stored in this field. |- ! Phone No | The phone number of the partner can be stored in this field. . |}
'''Transaction Status''': Support is added to provide visibility within Acumatica to see when documents have been sent to the Trading Partner. {| cellspacing="0" cellpadding="4" border="1" |-style="text-align: center; background-color: #D0D0D0; " !Field !! Description |- ! Advanced Ship Notice Status | UDF in Shipmnent to indicate the sent status of Advanced Ship Notice(856) in Transaction Manager. |}

==Batch Label Printing== Form ID: ([~/?ScreenId=TC503000|TC503000]) {br}
Batch Label Printing allows to batch print the labels for the packages and the pallets you selected.
{| cellspacing="0" cellpadding="4" border="1" |- | colspan="2" style="text-align: center; background-color: #D0D0D0; " | '''Batch Label Printing''' |- ! Shipment Number From | The first document number that you'd like to be in your range of orders to process. |- ! Shipment Number To |The last document number that you'd like to be in your range of orders to process. |- ! Date From | The first date that you'd like to be in your range of orders to process. |- ! Date To |The last date that you'd like to be in your range of orders to process. |- | rowspan="9" style="text-align: center;" | '''Doc Status''' | Open |- | Hold |- | Completed |- | Cancelled |- | Confirmed |- | Invoiced |- | Receipted |- | Auto-Generated |- | Partially Invoiced |- ! Purchase Order Number |The purchase order number. |- ! EDI Distribution Center |The EDI distribution center from the inbound purchase order. |- ! Customer |The customer number. |- ! Label Partner |The label partner. |- ! Level |Pack, Pallet and Both. |- ! Label Template |If setup, labels will be printed based on this template. Corresponding UDF in shipment will be updated as well. Available when only one partner's labels are selected. |- ! ASN Type |If setup, labels xml will be generated in this structure and printed. Corresponding UDF in shipment will be updated as well. Available when only one partner's labels are selected. |- ! Validate Required Field |True if to perform the required fields check before printing. It will return error details if the template chosen in the above option “Label Template” has required fields but empty mapping values. This will override the option “Validate Required Field” in TC Customer Settings. |- ! Print Destination |Select a printer that has been configured using the Acumatica Device Hub for label printing. |}

==Process Shipment== Form ID: ([~/?ScreenId=TC502020|TC502020]) {br}
Process Shipment allows to check if the shipments you selected have been sent to your trading partners as an Advanced Ship Notice. This process can be initiated by selecting an order and/or date range. TrueCommerce defined an inactive automation schedule that can be executed every 1 hour. You can process these transactions manually or by the automation schedule.
{| cellspacing="0" cellpadding="4" border="1" |- | colspan="2" style="text-align: center; background-color: #D0D0D0; " | '''Process Shipment''' |- ! Document Number From | The first document number that you'd like to be in your range of shipments to process. |- ! Document Number To |The last document number that you'd like to be in your range of shipments to process. |- ! Date From | The first date that you'd like to be in your range of shipments to process. |- ! Date To |The last date that you'd like to be in your range of shipments to process. |}

==Invoices== Form ID: ([~/?ScreenId=SO303000|SO303000]) {br}
====Document Details Tab==== TrueCommerce has added the PO Line Number as well as three User Defined Fields to the Document Details tab of the Sales Order screen. These three fields provide storage location to which you can transfer data from Transaction Manager to Acumatica.
As part of this integration to Acumatica when transactions are exported from Transaction Manager to Acumatica, fields are passed to Acumatica with data that Acumatica doesn’t normally store.
{| cellspacing="0" cellpadding="4" border="1" |-style="text-align: center; background-color: #D0D0D0; " !Field !! Description |- ! User Define Fields(1-3) | Any additional information that is sent in the inbound purchase order that is pertinent to your business can be stored in these user defined fields. |- ! PO Line Number | The line number from the inbound purchase order. |} ====TrueCommerce Tab====
'''TrueCommerce UDF''': The TrueCommerce UDF section on the Invoices screen lists the fields that were originally passed from Transaction Manager to Acumatica during the sales order creation. With the exception of the Purchase Order Number field, there currently is no standard matching field within Acumatica for the EDI Store Number and EDI Distribution Center. Therefore, TrueCommerce UDF section has been added to the Integration with Acumatica to store this data. Additionally, five user defined fields have also been added to this section as the storage location to which customers can transfer data from Transaction Manager to Acumatica.
{| cellspacing="0" cellpadding="4" border="1" |-style="text-align: center; background-color: #D0D0D0; " !Field !! Description |- ! Purchase Order | The purchase order number can be stored in this field. |- ! EDI Store Number |The EDI store number from the inbound purchase order can be stored to Acumatica in this field. |- ! EDI Distribution Center | The EDI distribution center from the inbound purchase order can be stored to Acumatica in this field. |- ! User Defined Fields (1-5) | Any additional information that is sent in the inbound purchase order that is pertinent to your business can be stored in these user defined fields. |- ! Master Tracking # | This field automatically retrieves the first tracking number listed on the Shipment to be included on the Invoice. If multiple Shipments are included on the Invoice then the first tracking number in the series will appear in this field. |}
'''Transaction Status''': Support is added to provide visibility within Acumatica to see when documents have been sent to the Trading Partner. {| cellspacing="0" cellpadding="4" border="1" |-style="text-align: center; background-color: #D0D0D0; " !Field !! Description |- ! Invoice SO Status | UDF in Invoice to indicate the sent status of Invoice SO(810) in Transaction Manager. |}

==Process Sales Order Invoice== Form ID: ([~/?ScreenId=TC502060|TC502060]) {br}
Process Sales Order Invoice allows to check if the sales orders you selected have been sent to your trading partners as a Sales Order Invoice. This process can be initiated by selecting an order and/or date range. TrueCommerce defined an inactive automation schedule that can be executed every 1 hour. You can process these transactions manually or by the automation schedule.
{| cellspacing="0" cellpadding="4" border="1" |- | colspan="2" style="text-align: center; background-color: #D0D0D0; " | '''Process Sales Order Invoice''' |- ! Document Number From | The first document number that you'd like to be in your range of invoices to process. |- ! Document Number To |The last document number that you'd like to be in your range of invoices to process. |- ! Date From | The first date that you'd like to be in your range of invoices to process. |- ! Date To |The last date that you'd like to be in your range of invoices to process. |}

