==TrueCommerce Activity Report==
Form ID:  ([~/?ScreenId=TC.64.00.40|TC.64.00.40]) {br}    

TrueCommerce Activity Report4 displays the Pulse Dashboard after you log on Foundry.

==Report Service== Form ID: ([~/?ScreenId=TC103030|TC103030]) {br}
The Report Service window provides the ability to enter the correct URL of the Embedded Analytics API.
{| cellspacing="0" cellpadding="4" border="1" |- | colspan="2" style="text-align: center; background-color: #D0D0D0; " | '''Report Service''' |- ! Service URL | This field will be set after getting the correct URL of the Embedded Analytics API from TrueCommerce. |}

==Process Invoice AR== Form ID: ([~/?ScreenId=TC502030|TC502030]) {br}
Process Invoice AR allows to check if the invoices you selected have been sent to your trading partners as an Invoice AR. This process can be initiated by selecting an order and/or date range. TrueCommerce defined an inactive automation schedule that can be executed every 1 hour. You can process these transactions manually or by the automation schedule.
{| cellspacing="0" cellpadding="4" border="1" |- | colspan="2" style="text-align: center; background-color: #D0D0D0; " | '''Process Invoice AR''' |- ! Document Number From | The first document number that you'd like to be in your range of invoices to process. |- ! Document Number To |The last document number that you'd like to be in your range of invoices to process. |- ! Date From | The first date that you'd like to be in your range of invoices to process. |- ! Date To |The last date that you'd like to be in your range of invoices to process. |}

WikiRevision.column:
==Labeling Customer Settings== Form ID: ([~/?ScreenId=TC102010|TC102010]) {br}
The Labeling Customer Settings window provides the ability to set the label partner, template, GS1-128, ship-from address and label field maps for each customer to print labels. The label partner and template populate based on the customer having the trading partner and label template deployed to their Transaction Manager instance.
====General Settings====
{| cellspacing="0" cellpadding="4" border="1" |- | colspan="2" style="text-align: center; background-color: #D0D0D0; " | '''Labeling Customer Settings''' |- ! Refresh Partner and Template | Click the button to get the latest Label Partners and Templates for your tenant. |- ! Customer ID | This is the Acumatica Customer ID. |- ! Default Ship-from Address | The default Ship-from Address for this customer. |- ! Default Label Partner | The default Label Partner for this customer. |- ! Default Label Template | The default Label Template for this customer. |- | rowspan ="2" style="text-align: center" | '''Continue label printing when item line sequence mismatches''' | '''Ignore''' - Continue label printing if the order is not coming from Transaction Manager. |- | '''Error''' - Error on label printing if the order is not coming from Transaction Manager. |- | rowspan ="2" style="text-align: center" | '''Continue label printing when GS1-128 code is invalid''' | '''Ignore''' - Ignore the packages whose GS1-128(s) are invalid and continue label printing for the packages whose GS1-128(s) are valid. |- | '''Error''' - Error on label printing if any invalid GS1-128(s) exists. |- ! Validate Required Fields | An option to decide if you need to validate the required fields when printing the labels. |- ! Pull Ship-from Address from Location on Shipment | An option to decide if you need to pull ship-from address from Location on Shipment when printing the labels. |- ! Next GS1-128 # | This is the Next GS1-128 number generated by Extension, Company # and Next Serial #. |- ! Extension | The extension number of the GS1-128. |- ! Company # | The company number of the GS1-128. |- ! Next Serial # | The next serial number of the GS1-128. |- ! Generate GS1-128 Auto-Create | An option that control if you need to auto-generate the GS1-128. |- ! Print Destination | Select a printer that has been configured using the Acumatica Device Hub for label printing. |} ====Label Field Maps==== With the ability to print labels from within Acumatica, we will still be using the default Transaction Manager label templates. There is added functionality to Acumatica that will allow the user to override the default label mapping. In addition, there is added functionality to retrieve compliancy data from the originating order in Transaction Manager. Please note, any changes you make to the labels could impact compliancy with your trading partner. Fields you set here will overwrite the default.
{| cellspacing="0" cellpadding="4" border="1" |- | colspan="2" style="text-align: center; background-color: #D0D0D0; " | '''Label Field Maps''' |- ! Load Label Field | When the customer clicks this button, Acumatica will call Label API to get label template variables (Label Fields), ASN Transaction Types which has setup import document type in TM and corresponding Misc token captions of that transaction type. Then insert into corresponding table in Acumatica. |- ! Load Acumatica Field | When the customer clicks this button, any changes to Acumatica Tables/Acumatica Fields will be refreshed. |- ! Transaction Type | Select the ASN Transaction Type according to the Label Partner and Template to update Misc token captions. |- ! Label Field | Label Fields are synced from the label API. User can map Label Fields according to Label Template manually or Load Label Fields automatically via Load Label Fields button. |- ! Length | The length of the Label Field. |- ! Used | An attribute of Label Field. It means if this field is used in the label template. |- ! Required | An attribute of Label Field. It means if this field is required in the label template. |- ! Level | The level of Label Field. It means which nodes the label field is under in the label xml. |- ! Acumatica Table | This is the Acumatica table you want to map the label field from. |- ! Acumatica Field | This is the Acumatica Field you want to map the label field from. |}

==Process Warehouse Shipping Order== Form ID: ([~/?ScreenId=TC502050|TC502050]) {br}
Process Warehouse Shipping Order allows to check if the sales orders you selected have been sent to your trading partners as a Warehouse Shipping Order. This process can be initiated by selecting an order and/or date range. TrueCommerce defined an inactive automation schedule that can be executed every 1 hour. You can process these transactions manually or by the automation schedule.
{| cellspacing="0" cellpadding="4" border="1" |- | colspan="2" style="text-align: center; background-color: #D0D0D0; " | '''Process Warehouse Shipping Order'' |- ! Document Number From | The first document number that you'd like to be in your range of orders to process. |- ! Document Number To |The last document number that you'd like to be in your range of orders to process. |- ! Date From | The first date that you'd like to be in your range of orders to process. |- ! Date To |The last date that you'd like to be in your range of orders to process. |}

