WikiRevision.column:
==Process Shipment Automation== Form ID: ([~/?ScreenId=TC501000|TC501000]) {br}
Process Shipment Automation allows for the creation of multiple shipments at once. This process can be initiated by selecting an order and/or date range. You can choose to either create only the shipment or create the shipment and auto-pack at the same time.
{| cellspacing="0" cellpadding="4" border="1" |- | colspan="2" style="text-align: center; background-color: #D0D0D0; " | '''Process Shipment Automation''' |- ! From Sales Order Number | The first sales order number that you'd like to be in your range of orders to process shipments for. If you wish to process shipments for a single order, just enter a single sales order number in either the "From Sales Order Number" or "To Sales Order Number" field. |- ! To Sales Order Number |The last sales order number that you'd like to be in your range of orders to process shipments for. If you wish to process shipments for a single order, just enter one a single sales order number in either the "From Sales Order Number" or "To Sales Order Number" field. |- ! From Date | The first date that you'd like to be in your range of orders to process shipments for. If you wish to process shipments for a single day, just enter one a single date in either the "From Date" or "To Date" field. |- ! To Date |The last date that you'd like to be in your range of orders to process shipments for. If you wish to process shipments for a single day, just enter one a single date in either the "From Date" or "To Date" field. |- ! Auto Pack |This dropdown menu provides you with the option to either create only the Shipment or create both the Shipment and Auto-Pack at the same time. |- ! Confirm Shipment |Check this box if you’d like to change the status of the Shipment to "Confirmed" after creating the Shipment or the Shipment and Auto-Packing the items. |}

==Sales Orders== Form ID: ([~/?ScreenId=SO301000|SO301000]) {br}
====Document Details Tab==== TrueCommerce has added the PO Line Number as well as three User Defined Fields to the Document Details tab of the Sales Order screen. These three fields provide storage location to which you can transfer data from Transaction Manager to Acumatica.
As part of this integration to Acumatica when transactions are exported from Transaction Manager to Acumatica, fields are passed to Acumatica with data that Acumatica doesn’t normally store.
{| cellspacing="0" cellpadding="4" border="1" |-style="text-align: center; background-color: #D0D0D0; " !Field !! Description |- ! User Define Fields(1-3) | Any additional information that is sent in the inbound purchase order that is pertinent to your business can be stored in these user defined fields. |- ! PO Line Number | The line number from the inbound purchase order. |} ====TrueCommerce Tab==== '''TrueCommerce UDF''': The TrueCommerce UDF section on the Sales Orders screen lists the fields that are passed from Transaction Manager to Acumatica and populate to the TrueCommerce tab on an Acumatica Sales Order or Quote. With the exception of the Purchase Order Number field, there currently is no standard matching field within Acumatica for the EDI Store Number and EDI Distribution Center. Therefore, the TrueCommerce UDF section has been added to the Integration with Acumatica to store this data. Additionally, five user defined fields have also been added to this section as the storage location to which customers can transfer data from Transaction Manager to Acumatica.
As part of this integration to Acumatica when transactions are exported from Transaction Manager to Acumatica, fields are passed to Acumatica with data that Acumatica doesn’t normally store.
{| cellspacing="0" cellpadding="4" border="1" |-style="text-align: center; background-color: #D0D0D0; " !Field !! Description |- ! Purchase Order | The purchase order number can be stored in this field. |- ! EDI Store Number |The EDI store number from the inbound purchase order can be stored to Acumatica in this field. |- ! EDI Distribution Center | The EDI distribution center from the inbound purchase order can be stored to Acumatica in this field. |- ! User Defined Fields (1-5) | Any additional information that is sent in the inbound purchase order that is pertinent to your business can be stored in these user defined fields. |- | rowspan="10" style="text-align: center;" | '''ASN Type''' | No Pack - There is a no pack level defined on the ASN. |- |Pick & Pack - More than one product is placed into a single shipping container. |- |Standard - When standard is chosen, only one item type is allocated per shipping container. |- |Pallet Pick & Pack - More than one product is placed into a single pallet. |- |Pallet Standard - When standard is chosen, only one item type is allocated per pallet. |- |Pacejet Cloud No Pack - There is a no pack level defined on the ASN. (For Pacejet Integration) |- |Pacejet Cloud Pick & Pack - More than one product is placed into a single shipping container. (For Pacejet Integration) |- |Pacejet Cloud Standard - When standard is chosen, only one item type is allocated per shipping container. (For Pacejet Integration) |- |Pacejet Cloud Pallet Pick & Pack - More than one product is placed into a single pallet. (For Pacejet Integration) |- |Pacejet Cloud Pallet Standard - When standard is chosen, only one item type is allocated per pallet. (For Pacejet Integration) |- ! Revision Number |This UDF is used to maintain/track the Sales Order revision number to be used when sending the Sales Order to the Customer. |- ! Label Partner |During the Sales Order creation it’s possible to pass these values in when exporting a Purchase Order from Transaction Manager. It will be brought to Shipment from Sales Order. |- ! Label Template |During the Sales Order creation it’s possible to pass these values in when exporting a Purchase Order from Transaction Manager. It will be brought to Shipment from Sales Order. |- ! Print Destination |Select a printer that has been configured using the Acumatica Device Hub for label printing. |}
'''Ship-from Address''': The Ship From Address for label printing can be set when creating the sales order during the PO export from TM. It will be brought to Shipment from Sales Order.
{| cellspacing="0" cellpadding="4" border="1" |-style="text-align: center; background-color: #D0D0D0; "" !Field !! Description |- ! Name | The name of the partner can be stored in this field. |- ! Address Line 1 | The address of the partner can be stored in this field. |- ! Address Line 2 | The address of the partner can be stored in this field. |- ! City | The city of the partner can be stored in this field. |- ! Country | The country of the partner can be stored in this field. |- ! State | The state of the partner can be stored in this field. |- ! Postal Code | The postal code of the partner can be stored in this field. |- ! Phone No | The phone number of the partner can be stored in this field. |}
'''Transaction Status''': Support is added to provide visibility within Acumatica to see when documents have been sent to the Trading Partner. {| cellspacing="0" cellpadding="4" border="1" |-style="text-align: center; background-color: #D0D0D0; " !Field !! Description |- ! Purchase Order Acknowledgement Status | UDF in Sales Order to indicate the sent status of Purchase Order Acknowledgement(855) in Transaction Manager. |- ! Sales Order Invoice Status | UDF in Sales Order to indicate the sent status of Sales Order Invoice(810) in Transaction Manager. |- ! Warehouse Shipping Order Status | UDF in Sales Order to indicate the sent status of Warehouse Shipping Order(940) in Transaction Manager. |- ! Warehouse Shipping Order Revision Number Sent | UDF in Sales Order to indicate the max revision number of the sent Warehouse Shipping Order(940) in Transaction Manager. |}

==Process Purchase Order== Form ID: ([~/?ScreenId=TC502040|TC502040]) {br}
Process Purchase Order allows to check if the purchase orders you selected have been sent to your trading partners as a Purchase Order. This process can be initiated by selecting an order and/or date range. TrueCommerce defined an inactive automation schedule that can be executed every 1 hour. You can process these transactions manually or by the automation schedule.
{| cellspacing="0" cellpadding="4" border="1" |- | colspan="2" style="text-align: center; background-color: #D0D0D0; " | '''Process Purchase Order''' |- ! Document Number From | The first document number that you'd like to be in your range of orders to process. |- ! Document Number To |The last document number that you'd like to be in your range of orders to process. |- ! Date From | The first date that you'd like to be in your range of orders to process. |- ! Date To |The last date that you'd like to be in your range of orders to process. |}

