==Report Settings== Form ID: ([~/?ScreenId=TC103020|TC103020]) {br}
The Report Settings window provides the ability for the customer who want to use the Embedded Analytic Report to configure dashboard name and the KPIs in their reports. There are 10 reports can be customized by customers.
{| cellspacing="0" cellpadding="4" border="1" |- | colspan="2" style="text-align: center; background-color: #D0D0D0; " | '''Report Settings''' |- ! Report ID | This field is read-only and represents the primary key in the data table. |- ! Report Menu Name | This is the Report Menu Name which you set for the reports screen in the Site Map screen. This field is read-only. |- ! Company Name | This is the company you specified in your Pulse. TrueCommerce will find the Dashboards and the KPIs in you Pulse according to the Company Name and Product Name. |- ! Product Name | This field is the product in Pulse/Key Performance Indicators (KPIs) that are used to indicate the data source. |- ! Dashboard Name | This field represents the Pulse Dashboard Name. |}

==Item Package Settings== Form ID: ([~/?ScreenId=TC101000|TC101000]) {br}
The Item Package Settings screen is where you define the Pack Quantity for each Acumatica item that will be ordered and packaged for your trading partners. The pack quantity represents the total quantity of an item fits into a package. This value will be used for all customers when packaging shipments. If a customer has different packaging rules, you’ll need to setup an Auto-Pack Template for each customer that is unique. This list can be filtered by entering an Inventory ID in the text box or by clicking on the magnifying glass and selecting an item.
{| cellspacing="0" cellpadding="4" border="1" |- | colspan="2" style="text-align: center; background-color: #D0D0D0; " | '''Item Package Settings''' |- ! Inventory ID | The unique inventory ID from Acumatica. |- ! Description |The item description from Acumatica. |- ! Pack Quantity | The maximum quantity to be packaged within each box. |- ! Sales Unit |The unit of measure for the item. |- ! Default Price | The default price for the item. |- ! Weight |The weight of the item. |}

==Invoices and Memos== Form ID: ([~/?ScreenId=AR301000|AR301000]) {br}
====Document Details Tab==== TrueCommerce has added the PO Line Number as well as three User Defined Fields to the Document Details tab of the Sales Order screen. These three fields provide storage location to which you can transfer data from Transaction Manager to Acumatica.
As part of this integration to Acumatica when transactions are exported from Transaction Manager to Acumatica, fields are passed to Acumatica with data that Acumatica doesn’t normally store.
{| cellspacing="0" cellpadding="4" border="1" |-style="text-align: center; background-color: #D0D0D0; " !Field !! Description |- ! User Define Fields(1-3) | Any additional information that is sent in the inbound purchase order that is pertinent to your business can be stored in these user defined fields. |- ! PO Line Number | The line number from the inbound purchase order. |} ====TrueCommerce Tab====
'''TrueCommerce UDF''': The TrueCommerce UDF section on the Invoices and Memos screen lists the fields that were originally passed from Transaction Manager to Acumatica during the sales order creation. With the exception of the Purchase Order Number field, there currently is no standard matching field within Acumatica for the EDI Store Number and EDI Distribution Center. Therefore, the TrueCommerce UDF section has been added to the Integration with Acumatica to store this data. Additionally, five user defined fields have also been added to this section as the storage location to which customers can transfer data from Transaction Manager to Acumatica.
{| cellspacing="0" cellpadding="4" border="1" |-style="text-align: center; background-color: #D0D0D0; " !Field !! Description |- ! Purchase Order | The purchase order number can be stored in this field. |- ! EDI Store Number |The EDI store number from the inbound purchase order can be stored to Acumatica in this field. |- ! EDI Distribution Center | The EDI distribution center from the inbound purchase order can be stored to Acumatica in this field. |- ! User Defined Fields (1-5) | Any additional information that is sent in the inbound purchase order that is pertinent to your business can be stored in these user defined fields. |- ! Master Tracking # | This field automatically retrieves the first tracking number listed on the Shipment to be included on the Invoice. If multiple Shipments are included on the Invoice then the first tracking number in the series will appear in this field. |}
'''Transaction Status''': Support is added to provide visibility within Acumatica to see when documents have been sent to the Trading Partner. {| cellspacing="0" cellpadding="4" border="1" |-style="text-align: center; background-color: #D0D0D0; " !Field !! Description |- ! Invoice AR Status | UDF in Invoice and Memo to indicate the sent status of Invoice AR(810) in Transaction Manager. |}

