WikiRevision.column:
==Customizations==
TrueCommerce has made modifications to the user interface in order to accommodate order information that may not be traditionally stored within standard Acumatica’s screens.  These modifications allow for the compliancy data points to be include on outbound documents to trading partners.  These data points can be created during the export of an order or through manual entry.
==New Functionality==
'''__Sales Order__ '''{br}
On the Sales Order screen TrueCommerce has added a new tab titled “TrueCommerce” which holds critical order data points such as the Purchase Order Number, EDI Store Number, EDI Distribution Center as well as five additional user defined fields (UDFs) that can mapped from an inbound document to Acumatica. {br}
  {br}
'''__Invoice__ '''{br}
On the Invoices screen TrueCommerce has added a new tab titled “TrueCommerce” which holds critical order data points such as the Purchase Order Number, EDI Store Number, EDI Distribution Center as well as five additional user defined fields (UDFs) that if mapped from an inbound purchase order can be carried over to the invoice. {br}
{br}
'''__Invoice and Memos__ '''{br}
On the Invoices screen TrueCommerce has added a new tab titled “TrueCommerce” which holds critical order data points such as the Purchase Order Number, EDI Store Number, EDI Distribution Center as well as five additional user defined fields (UDFs) that if mapped from an inbound purchase order can be carried over to the invoice. {br}
  {br}
'''__Shipments__''' {br}
On the Shipments screen TrueCommerce has added a new tab titled “TrueCommerce” which holds critical order data points such as the Purchase Order Number, EDI Store Number, EDI Distribution Center as well as five additional user defined fields (UDFs) that if mapped from an inbound purchase order can be carried over to the shipment. {br}
  {br}
'''__Auto-Pack Template__ '''{br}
Auto-Pack Template screen (located under TrueCommerce on the Sales Orders menu) allows you to define special packaging rules that can then be assigned to Acumatica customers.  You can define packaging rules by Pack Quantity and can set rules to package multiple items to a carton. {br}
  {br}
'''__Item Package Settings__ '''{br}
The Item Package Settings screen (located under TrueCommerce on the Sales Orders menu) is where you define the Pack Quantity for each Acumatica item that will be ordered and packaged for your trading partners. {br}
{br}
'''__Customer Settings__ '''{br}
The Customer Settings screen (located under TrueCommerce on the Sales Orders menu) provides the ability to assign an Auto-Pack Template (created in the Auto-Pack Template screen) to specific customer(s) to be used when creating packages for Shipments. {br}
{br}
'''__Process Shipment Automation__ '''{br}
The Process Shipment Automation screen (located under TrueCommerce on the Sales Orders menu) allows for the creation of multiple shipments at once. {br}
{br}
'''__Purchase Order__ '''{br}
On the Purchase Order screen TrueCommerce has added a new tab titled “TrueCommerce” which holds critical order data points such as the TC Status as well as five additional user defined fields (UDFs) that can mapped from an inbound document to Acumatica. {br}
{br}
'''__Purchase Receipt__ '''{br}
On the Purchase Receipt screen TrueCommerce has added a new tab titled “TrueCommerce” which holds five additional user defined fields (UDFs)  that can mapped from an inbound document to Acumatica. {br}
{br}
'''__Bills and Adjustments__ '''{br}
On the Bills and Adjustments screen TrueCommerce has added a new tab titled “TrueCommerce” which holds five additional user defined fields (UDFs)  that can mapped from an inbound document to Acumatica. {br}
{br}
'''__Report Settings__ '''{br}
The Report Settings screen allows you to update the dashboard information according to the dashboard you set in the Pulse. {br}
{br}
'''__TrueCommerce Activity Report__ '''{br}
The first time you access to this screen, TrueCommerce will ask you to login with your Foundry credentials. After you login, you need to re-access this screen. Then the TrueCommerce Activity Report screen will display a dashboard which we design in your Pulse. {br}
{br}
'''__TrueCommerce Activity Report2__ '''{br}
The first time you access to this screen, TrueCommerce will ask you to login with your Foundry credentials. After you login, you need to re-access this screen. Then the TrueCommerce Activity Report2 screen will display a dashboard which we design in your Pulse. {br}
{br}
'''__TrueCommerce Activity Report3__ '''{br}
The first time you access to this screen, TrueCommerce will ask you to login with your Foundry credentials. After you login, you need to re-access this screen. Then the TrueCommerce Activity Report3 screen will display a dashboard which we design in your Pulse. {br}
{br}
'''__TrueCommerce Activity Report4__ '''{br}
The first time you access to this screen, TrueCommerce will ask you to login with your Foundry credentials. After you login, you need to re-access this screen. Then the TrueCommerce Activity Report4 screen will display a dashboard which we design in your Pulse. {br}
{br}
