'''__Transaction Status Settings__ '''{br}
The Transaction Status Settings window provides the ability for the customer who want to use the Transaction Status Indicator to configure the default date range for the Transactions. Users must connect their Acumatica to Indicator API and Foundry using their Foundry user credentials.{br}
{br}
'''__Process Purchase Order Acknowledgement__ '''{br}
Process Purchase Order Acknowledgement allows to check if the sales orders you selected have been sent to your trading partners as a Purchase Order Acknowledgement. {br}
{br}
'''__Process Warehouse Shipping Order__ '''{br}
Process Warehouse Shipping Order allows to check if the sales orders you selected have been sent to your trading partners as a Warehouse Shipping Order. {br}
{br}
'''__Process Shipment__ '''{br}
Process Shipment allows to check if the shipments you selected have been sent to your trading partners as an Advanced Ship Notice.  {br}
{br}
'''__Process Invoice AR__ '''{br}
Process Invoice AR allows to check if the invoices you selected have been sent to your trading partners as an Invoice AR. {br}
{br}
'''__Process Invoice SO__ '''{br}
Process Invoice SO allows to check if the invoices you selected have been sent to your trading partners as an Invoice SO.{br}
{br}
'''__Process Sales Order Invoice__ '''{br}
Process Sales Order Invoice allows to check if the sales orders you selected have been sent to your trading partners as a Sales Order Invoice.{br}
{br}
'''__Process Purchase Order__ '''{br}
Process Purchase Order allows to check if the purchase orders you selected have been sent to your trading partners as a Purchase Order. {br}
{br}
'''__Labeling Settings__ '''{br}
The Labeling Settings window provides the ability for the customer who want to print Label for the shipments to configure the Label page size(Labels are split into batches of maximum of 100 labels per PDF), Label log Tracing and the number of days to log within, {br}
{br}
'''__Labeling Customer Settings__ '''{br}
The Labeling Customer Settings window provides the ability to set the label partner, template, GS1-128 and label field maps for each customer to print labels. {br}
{br}
'''__Ship-from Address__ '''{br}
A ship from address must be set in order to publish on the label. You need to specify for the customer, what address will print on the labels as the Ship-from address(TC105000), {br}
{br}
'''__Batch Label Printing__ '''{br}
Batch Label Printing allows to batch print the labels for the shipment you selected.{br}
{br}
'''__Labeling Log__ '''{br}
This form is to show the label logs if you fail to print a label, {br}
{br}
'''__Login__ '''{br}
You must connect you Acumatica to API and Foundry using their Foundry user credentials. TrueCommerce will check the SKU permission, get all the trading partner names and templates for the customer’s tenant based on their login.(The customer must have the labeling sku as part of their Transaction Manager instance) {br}
{br}
'''__API Urls__ '''{br}
The API Urls window is just for internal use. {br}
{br}
'''__Extension Version__ '''{br}
The Extension Version window  allows to check the extension version number. {br}
{br}

