==ASN Customer Settings== Form ID: ([~/?ScreenId=TC102000|TC102000]) {br}
The ASN Customer Settings window provides the ability to assign an Auto-Pack Template (created in the Auto-Pack Template screen) to specific customer(s) to be used when creating packages for Shipments.
{| cellspacing="0" cellpadding="4" border="1" |- | colspan="2" style="text-align: center; background-color: #D0D0D0; " | '''Customer Settings''' |- ! Customer ID | This is the Acumatica Customer ID. |- | rowspan ="10" style="text-align: center" | '''ASN Type''' | '''Pick & Pack''' - More than one product is placed into a single shipping container. |- |'''Standard''' - When standard is chosen, only one item type is allocated per shipping container. |- | '''No Pack''' - There is a no pack level defined on the ASN. |- | '''Pallet Pick & Pack''' - More than one product is placed into a single pallet. |- | '''Pallet Standard''' - When standard is chosen, only one item type is allocated per pallet. |- |'''Pacejet Cloud No Pack''' - There is a no pack level defined on the ASN. (For Pacejet Integration) |- |'''Pacejet Cloud Pick & Pack''' - More than one product is placed into a single shipping container. (For Pacejet Integration) |- |'''Pacejet Cloud Standard''' - When standard is chosen, only one item type is allocated per shipping container. (For Pacejet Integration) |- |'''Pacejet Cloud Pallet Pick''' & Pack - More than one product is placed into a single pallet. (For Pacejet Integration) |- |'''Pacejet Cloud Pallet Standard''' - When standard is chosen, only one item type is allocated per pallet. (For Pacejet Integration) |- | rowspan ="2" style="text-align: center" | '''Auto Pack Type''' | '''Pure Carton''' - Only like items are packaged together. |- | '''Mix Carton''' - Different items can be packaged together (this option must be used if you wish to assign a template to a specific customer). |- ! Template ID |The name of the Auto-Pack Template you wish to assign to this customer (previously made in the Auto-Pack Template screen). |}
